{%- comment -%}
  Wholesale — "Proudly Bringing You the Best"

  A 1:1 port of the band from the Replo wholesale page
  (snippets/reploChunk.b817892c-*.liquid). The markup and the CSS below are
  Replo's own, so the rendering matches the live page exactly; only the copy,
  the images and the section padding are lifted into settings.

  Replo ships a desktop tree and a separate mobile tree and toggles them by
  media query — both are kept, and both read the same settings, so editing a
  point updates both.

  Every selector is prefixed with #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} so the
  Replo class hashes cannot leak into the rest of the theme, and the reset is
  scoped to .wsp-proudly rather than the document.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- style -%}
/* Kill any margin/padding the theme puts on section wrappers - the Replo
   markup already carries its own vertical rhythm. */
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
/* Replo's reset. Deliberately NOT prefixed with #shopify-section-... : the ported
   Replo rules below carry that prefix (id-level specificity), and in the original
   page they outranked this reset via Replo's `:not(#)` hack. Keeping the reset
   at class-level specificity reproduces that order - it still beats the theme's
   base styles, but loses to Replo's own padding, border and font-size. */
.wsp-proudly *,
.wsp-proudly *::before,
.wsp-proudly *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
.wsp-proudly [data-rid] {
  margin: 0; padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: 100%;
  vertical-align: baseline; letter-spacing: inherit;
}
/* Replo puts the type on the wrapper div and leaves the heading/paragraph inside
   it unstyled - and those tags carry no data-rid, so the reset above misses them.
   That let the browser's default margin-block (h1 .67em, p 1em) and the theme's
   heading sizes leak in. Zero the box and let every font property inherit from
   Replo's wrapper. <strong> is deliberately left out so bold survives. */
.wsp-proudly h1,
.wsp-proudly h2,
.wsp-proudly h3,
.wsp-proudly h4,
.wsp-proudly h5,
.wsp-proudly h6,
.wsp-proudly p,
.wsp-proudly ul,
.wsp-proudly ol,
.wsp-proudly li {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: inherit;
  font-weight: inherit;
  font-style: inherit;
  line-height: inherit;
  letter-spacing: inherit;
  color: inherit;
}

.wsp-proudly a { text-decoration: none; }
.wsp-proudly img { display: block; max-width: 100%; }

/* This one is settings-driven, so it must beat Replo's own 100px band padding -
   hence the id prefix. */
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .wsp-proudly > div {
  background-color: {{ section.settings.background_color }};
  padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
  padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
}
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .wsp-proudly > div {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top_mobile }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom_mobile }}px;
  }
}
